On 7 July 2010 16:57, Pierre Abbat <phma@phma.optus.nu> wrote:

> And there is no such thing as
> an adjective in Lojban.
>

But what does an adjective do to a noun? It modifies as a dependent. And
that's quite analogous with how a seltau relates to a tertau in a sumti-fied
tanru in Lojban. A tanru is closer than a NOI clause to the natlang
"adjective + noun", in my opinion.

